<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henri de La Tour d'Auvergne, Viscount of Turenne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1611">1611</a>–<a href="/years/1675">1675</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Viscount of Turenne</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henri de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-la-tour-dauvergne">La Tour d'Auvergne</a>, Viscount of Turenne, was one of the greatest French generals, born at Sedan, the son of its sovereign prince. He commanded in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-fronde">Fronde</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-dutch-war">Franco-Dutch War</a>, becoming Marshal General of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. His winter campaign of 1674 to 1675, ending at Turckheim, secured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>; he was killed at Salzbach in 1675.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henri-de-la-tour-d-auvergne-viscount-of-turenne.jpg" alt="Henri de La Tour d'Auvergne, Viscount of Turenne" width="320" height="376" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Circle of Philippe de Champaigne · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henri_de_la_Tour_d%27Auvergne,_Vicomte_de_Turenne_by_Circle_of_Philippe_de_Champaigne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
